 "notes": "Continuation page (printed page 257), no header; same 12 figure columns + Remarks (count checked). Top block (Gojari, Pahari, Panjabi, Chabhali, Pothwari) is braced 'Jammu Province' and continues the Jammu Province block begun on leaf 266 (Dogri, Kashmiri). No district-total rows. Jammu District: Jammu Tehsil (6 MTs); 'Ranbirsinghpura ,,' (ditto = Tehsil) Panjabi only; 'Samba ,,' and 'Akhnoor ,,' printed with all columns nil (omitted). Kathua District: Kathua Tehsil (Kashmiri, Pahari); Basohli Tehsil and Jasmergarh Tehsil all nil (omitted). Udhampur District: Udhampur Tehsil (Kashmiri, Pahari); Ramnagar Tehsil all nil (omitted); Ramban Tehsil (Dogri, Kashmiri, Gojari, Panjabi, Pahari) - the Udhampur District brace ends at the foot of the page, but whether the district continues on leaf 268 is decided by that leaf's labels. Ramban remarks use printed ditto marks (',,') standing for 'speaking 3 languages'; they are kept as printed: '8 males ,, ,, ,,' and '4/4/3 ,, ,, ,, ,,' (the first ditto stands for 'males'). Udhampur Tehsil Pahari mother-tongue persons: the first digit is damaged in the print but reads 3,913 = 2,073 + 1,840. Remarks checked against the figures: all agree. The Gojari and Pahari (Jammu Province) pair letters (B = Dogri, C = Panjabi, D = Kashmiri) reconcile exactly with the columns. Jammu Tehsil Chabhali says 'One person' and the Ranbirsinghpura Panjabi remark also says 'One person'; the figures show one male in each. Cross-check with Part II(A): leaf0255.json has Ramban Kashmiri MT persons 31,036. This leaf prints 31,936 clearly (checked under zoom), which equals 17,151 + 14,785, so the Part A value is the one to re-check."
